# Line endings: LF in the repository, and LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference. A Windows clone with git's default `core.autocrlf=true` checks the tree out
# as CRLF, and then `cargo fmt --check` fails on files nobody touched, byte-exact fixtures stop
# matching, and a contributor's first commit rewrites every line of whatever they edited. `eol=lf`
# pins the checkout regardless of the user's own setting.
#
# The `text=auto` half also matters for what it *excludes*: a `.png`, a patched font, or the gzipped
# models.dev snapshot must never go through line-ending normalization, so they are marked explicitly.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.gz  binary
*.ttf binary

# Development-process artifacts — excluded from published release archives.
#
# These are Luxe's own planning spine, journal, and dogfooding memory. Luxe never
# *requires* them at runtime (every reader treats them as read-if-present), so a fresh
# consumer repo starts clean. `git archive` (and scripts/publish-clean.sh) drop them via
# the `export-ignore` attribute below; the files stay in this development repo for history.

# Careful: these are gitattributes patterns, NOT gitignore patterns. A trailing slash matches
# nothing here, so a directory has to be written `dir/**` or it silently ships anyway.
PROJECT.md          export-ignore
ROADMAP.md          export-ignore
PROGRESS.md         export-ignore
PLAN.md             export-ignore
docs/plan/**        export-ignore
docs/eval/**        export-ignore
docs/HANDOFF-*.md   export-ignore
.pi/**              export-ignore

# Loose working notes at the root: a review pass's findings, and third-party reference material that
# was never ours to redistribute.
luxe-review-findings.md export-ignore
shine-text.md       export-ignore

# Development scripts whose inputs are the export-ignored files above
scripts/tool-ergonomics.sh export-ignore
